refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns the time of the last modification of the current page. The value returned is a Unix timestamp, suitable for feeding to date. Returns &false; on error.
The value is computed once per request, the first time it is needed by getlastmod, getmyuid, getmygid or getmyinode (whichever is called first), and is then reused for the rest of the request. Unlike filemtime, this cached value is not affected by clearstatcache.

  &reftitle.examples;



    getlastmod example


<?php
// outputs e.g. 'Last modified: March 04 1998 20:43:59.'
echo "Last modified: " . date ("F d Y H:i:s.", getlastmod());
?>
